{{also|Kapellmeister}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|de|Kapellmeister}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|music}} A leader or [[conductor]] of a musical group such as an [[orchestra]].
#: {{syn|en|conductor|bandmaster}}
# {{lb|en|music|historical}} A term used during the [[baroque]] and [[classical|classical period]] for the person in charge of music at a noble [[court]].
#* '''2014''', Sterling E. Murray, ''The Career of an Eighteenth-Century Kapellmeister: The Life and Music of Antonio Rosetti'', Boydell & Brewer ({{ISBN|9781580464673}}), page 41:
#*: The daily routine of the Hofkapelle was normally entrusted to the '''Kapellmeister'''. This was the most important musical position at court.